<title>UK: Granada loses royal bid for hotels - paper.</title>
<headline>Granada loses royal bid for hotels - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Price disagreements are said to have led to Saudi billionaire Prince al-Waleed bin Talal dropping out of bidding for Granada Group's Exclusive hotels, the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 17 Exclusives, which have a book value of 801 million stg ($1.29 billion), include the Hotel Eden in Rome and the Ritz in Madrid.</p>
<p>However, the report said the prince may return to the negotiating table.</p>
</text>
